        <section id="network-security"  class="t-bg-primary">
          
            <h2>Network security</h2>
              <p>All networks should have security already in place but also having each computer with extra security helps to make this more resilient. Anti virus software should identify, block, and mitigate any targeted threats such as malware, ransomware and phishing but there are also additional ways to ensure networks are secure.</p>
<p>scroll through the slides below to learn more about these.</p>

              
              
<div class="gallery-container">
  <div role="group" class="gallery no-js">
    <ul>
        <li role="listitem">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Identity verification
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>Network security is usually based on strict identity verification processes with only authenticated and authorized users and devices being able to access applications and data. At the same time, it protects those applications and users from advanced threats on the Internet. Users and devices should be able to safely connect to the Internet, as long as they follow the network guidelines</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/cs/cs_u2_s1_p3_slide1.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </li>
        <li role="listitem">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Virtual Private Networks
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>VPN's or virtual private networks are encrypted connections over the internet from a device to a network. They help ensure that sensitive data is safely transmitted and traffic remains private allowing the user to work remotely. Smartphones and tablets can also connect through VPN.
Secure remote access also provides a safe and secure way to connect users and devices remotely to a corporate network. This includes VPN technology to authenticate the user or device.</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/cs/cs_u2_s1_p3_slide2.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

            
          
