        <h3>Creating networks</h3>
<p>The best way to learn about networks and their differences is to build one and Cisco have created a tool to do this. Cisco Packet Tracer is a tool built by Cisco to simulate a network. It is used to help students learn the principles of networking whilst gaining hands-on experience and develop Cisco technology skills. It doesn't involve the use of routers or switches but is purely a software only method. It uses packet trace to demonstrate technical concepts and networking systems. As a software it is also used by engineers to test any protocols before implementing them and try out any changes only deploying if everything works as expected.</p>
